                <pb facs="0740" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg620"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/5646: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany (Sackett) to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-05-12T15:00:00+01:00">May 12, 1932—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 12—10:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. Your 50, May 11, 6 p.m. Have seen Ministerial Director Ritter. Based on promising outlook of
                    negotiations in Washington as today reported by German Ambassador, I have reason
                    to believe favorable solution can be expected here. In spite of holidays matter
                    will be submitted to Cabinet for decision after Reichstag adjournment which is
                    expected today, and I hope to report definitely early next week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sackett</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
